subject: fix(smart-router): start sr-* combo cleanup scheduler from instrumentation.js

BUG: The optional stale smart-router combo sweep (settings.srComboCleanup.
enabled) never ran in the standalone build. sr-* combos accumulated
indefinitely even with the toggle enabled.

ROOT CAUSE: The scheduler was started from initializeApp(), which is
imported as a side-effect by src/app/layout.js via bootstrap.js. In the
Next.js 16 standalone build, that bootstrap chunk is tree-shaken — nothing
references it, so initializeApp() never runs. The markdown log flusher
avoids this by starting from src/instrumentation.js, which IS loaded in
standalone builds.

FIX (src/instrumentation.js): Start the sr-combo cleanup scheduler from
the instrumentation register() hook, gated on settings.srComboCleanup.
enabled (same condition as before). Fail-open: any error is logged and
swallowed.

VERIFICATION (production standalone via tray app, port 20130):
- Before: no [SR_CLEANUP] logs, sr-* combos never swept
- After: console buffer shows:
    [SR_CLEANUP] Scheduler started {"ttlHours":1,"intervalMs":3600000}
    [SR_CLEANUP] Deleted stale smart combo "sr-modelRouter-code-generation"
    [SR_CLEANUP] Deleted stale smart combo "sr-modelRouter-qa_knowledge"
    [SR_CLEANUP] Deleted stale smart combo "sr-modelRouter-summarization"
- All 3 stale combos (older than 1h TTL) deleted on the initial tick;
  fresh combos preserved.

FOUND BY: E2E verification of the sr-* cleanup toggle (item 4 of the
final testing pass). Documented in
learnings/2026-08-07-sr-cleanup-scheduler-standalone.md.

